{"availability":"available","full":"accius/openhamclock","name":"openhamclock","description":"\"The original HamClock will cease to function in June 2026. OpenHamClock aims to carry on Elwood's legacy with a modern, open-source implementation that the community can maintain and improve together.\"","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":464,"forks":144,"created":"2026-01-30T04:30:16Z","updated":"2026-09-27T01:30:14Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":null,"color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:55.312Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:55.312Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T05:48:55.312Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:37:40.938Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T21:18:29.706Z","stars":464,"forks":143},{"at":"2026-10-04T05:48:55.312Z","stars":464,"forks":144}],"technologies":["React","Three.js","Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A real-time amateur radio dashboard for the modern operator.","OpenHamClock brings DX cluster spots, space weather, propagation predictions, POTA/SOTA/WWFF/WWBOTA activations, PSKReporter, satellite tracking, WSJT-X integration, direct rig control, an in-browser logbook, and a full emergency-communications mode into a single browser-based interface. Run it locally on a Raspberry Pi, on your desktop, in Docker, or just use the hosted site.","📧 Contact: Chris, K0CJH — chris@cjhlighting.com"],"features":["Interactive world map in three projections — flat (Mercator), azimuthal-equidistant centered on your QTH, and a full 3D globe with real satellite models — with a dozen basemap styles and 28 toggleable overlay layers…","DX cluster spots from OpenHamClock's own cluster node (RBN + HamQTH + POTA/SOTA/WWFF + user spots, deduplicated), with band/mode/zone/watchlist filtering, worked-before and dupe badges from your log, click-to-tune, and…","Activations — live POTA, SOTA, WWFF, and WWBOTA activator panels with map markers.","Native logbook — QSOs stored in your browser (IndexedDB), ADIF import/export, log-from-spot, and worked-before integration across all spot panels.","Propagation — browser-side ITU-R P.533-14 (VOACAP-class) predictions via WebAssembly, point-to-point reliability charts, world heatmap, MUF map, band conditions, and ionosonde-corrected real-time data."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/accius/openhamclock/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0393e1000026882b4dc90f79350b720bf0018f6a13454d0ac6e85cecd6e8e3cd","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T05:59:26.946Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T06:13:19.482Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-27T01:30:14Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A real-time amateur radio dashboard for the modern operator.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/accius/openhamclock/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Self-host with Docker:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/accius/openhamclock/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"Self-host from source (Node.js 22 LTS recommended):","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/accius/openhamclock/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"A callsign makes PSKReporter \"my signal\" views and cluster login meaningful, but anyone can watch spots and space weather.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/accius/openhamclock/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"0393e1000026882b4dc90f79350b720bf0018f6a13454d0ac6e85cecd6e8e3cd","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/accius/openhamclock/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T06:13:19.483Z"},"enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T14:33:38.186Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v26.8.0 — Moonbounce, Zone-Scoped Openings, and an EmComm Week","tag":"v26.8.0","publishedAt":"2026-09-24T16:20:09Z","url":"https://github.com/accius/openhamclock/releases/tag/v26.8.0"},"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T14:33:38.186Z","screenshots":[],"overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T06:13:11.488Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1